{"author":{"id":"6af04b5756f10b3005a23338b8f25a6c1d7564fe1ddddc77e70806b2f14ac31a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789490275,"nonce":"VFa9D+fuJ00mTsbSMauU6Zvaj7E=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABRbl9iA","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/gic-lang/issues/30","origin":"github"},"title":"Add the deterministic Socratic tutor","message":"## Parent\n\ngit-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment\n\n## What to build\n\nDeliver the tutor pane end to end against a deterministic provider boundary. The tutor remains a soft dependency, sends context only after explicit submission, follows canonical Socratic guidance, and has no source-editing, write, shell, browser, or web tools.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Offline and unauthenticated states keep the pane visible with status, setup guidance, Retry, and Hide controls while every core IDE feature remains usable.\n- [ ] Editing, previewing, diagnostics, and runtime failures make no provider request before explicit student submission.\n- [ ] A submitted request contains the current source, diagnostics, runtime error, and structured output but no Canvas image.\n- [ ] The agent loads the canonical GIC tutor skill and bundled references and exposes no prohibited tools.\n- [ ] Tests pin context assembly, cancellation, streaming, provider failure, retry, and tool absence through a deterministic provider.\n- [ ] Response text and code-copy controls are unavailable in learning mode by default; one accessible setting restores normal selection and copying.\n- [ ] The UI does not claim deterministic enforcement of tutor prose or code length.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- git-bug issue `d2438d7` — Spike Pi providers and authentication in packaged Deno\n- git-bug issue `d5f66fd` — Build the resizable IDE workspace\n- git-bug issue `234820f` — Install and maintain the GIC tutor workspace","files":null}]}